---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Get Started - Choose the Right Isogun Labs Atlassian App"
  description="Choose the Isogun Labs Atlassian app that fits your workflow: Recap for Jira reporting, Field Hygiene for custom field cleanup, or Passdown for JSM handoffs."
  path="/get-started/"
>

<header class="page-hero chooser-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="kicker">Product chooser</div>
    <h1>Start with the workflow that is slowing your team down.</h1>
    <p>Three small Atlassian apps, each built for one clear job. Pick the problem you recognize and go straight to the app, docs, or Marketplace listing.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="block reveal chooser-block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chooser-grid">
      <article class="chooser-card">
        <div class="chooser-label">I need better status updates</div>
        <div class="top">
          <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 512 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M146,96 H330 L366,132 V396 H146 Z" fill="#C2610C"/><path d="M330,96 L366,132 H330 Z" fill="#7C3A08"/><rect x="174" y="186" width="164" height="18" rx="9" fill="#FDE7C7"/><rect x="174" y="228" width="164" height="18" rx="9" fill="#E8C39E"/><rect x="174" y="270" width="100" height="18" rx="9" fill="#E8C39E"/><circle cx="360" cy="390" r="52" fill="#15803D" stroke="#FFF" stroke-width="10"/><polyline points="336,392 354,410 388,368" fill="none" stroke="#FFF" stroke-width="14" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </span>
          <div>
            <div class="sub">Recap for Jira Cloud</div>
            <h3>Turn completed work into a monthly report.</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Best for engineers, product leads, and managers who need a clean written summary of what shipped without digging through Jira tickets manually.</p>
        <ul class="chooser-list">
          <li>One-click monthly reports from completed issues.</li>
          <li>Grouped by epic and written in plain past tense.</li>
          <li>Runs entirely on Atlassian and stores nothing.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="chooser-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-blue btn-sm" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/2146687861" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Marketplace</a>
          <a class="btn-text" href="https://recap.isogunlabs.com/">Product page</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="chooser-card">
        <div class="chooser-label">I need Jira admin cleanup</div>
        <div class="top">
          <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/field-hygiene-logo-144.png" alt="" /></span>
          <div>
            <div class="sub">Field Hygiene for Jira Cloud</div>
            <h3>Find custom field sprawl before it becomes debt.</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Best for Jira admins who need a fast read on duplicate fields, near-duplicates, unused fields, missing descriptions, and field-count pressure.</p>
        <ul class="chooser-list">
          <li>Duplicate and near-duplicate field detection.</li>
          <li>Warnings for type mismatches and missing descriptions.</li>
          <li>Read-only by design, with no setup flow.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="chooser-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-blue btn-sm" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/2905942594" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Marketplace</a>
          <a class="btn-text" href="https://field-hygiene.isogunlabs.com/">Product page</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="chooser-card">
        <div class="chooser-label">I need cleaner support handoffs</div>
        <div class="top">
          <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/passdown-logo-144.png" alt="" /></span>
          <div>
            <div class="sub">Passdown for JSM</div>
            <h3>Write shift handoffs automatically.</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Best for support teams using Jira Service Management schedules who want incoming agents to start with context, not detective work.</p>
        <ul class="chooser-list">
          <li>Detects shift boundaries from your JSM schedule.</li>
          <li>Posts a native comment with a plain-language brief.</li>
          <li>Mentions and assigns the incoming person automatically.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="chooser-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-blue btn-sm" href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3571155481" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Marketplace</a>
          <a class="btn-text" href="https://passdown.isogunlabs.com/">Product page</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta reveal">
  <div class="wrap cta-split">
    <div class="cta-copy">
      <h2>Not sure which one fits?</h2>
      <p>Send us the workflow that feels slow, repetitive, or risky. We will point you to the right app if it already exists, or tell you plainly if it does not.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-orange" href="mailto:support@isogunlabs.com">Talk with us</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/documentation/">Read the docs</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>